  "id": "lamenti_settimana_santa_sicilia",
  "name": "Lamenti della Settimana Santa (Sicilian Holy Week multipart laments)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Multipart Passion laments sung in Sicilian and in Latin by small groups of male singers, often linked to confraternities, during the processions and devotions of Holy Week, especially in the inland province of Caltanissetta. A leading voice carries the text while the others join on sustained chords, unaccompanied; Ignazio Macchiarella studied the practice and recorded the Montedoro singers for the Nota release 'Sicilia: La Settimana Santa a Montedoro' (1996).",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1990s lamenti della settimana santa, ritual Devotional, christian gospel branch, European funeral lament. a cappella small 3 to 8 one per part drone plus voices sustained pedal under melody sacred liturgical global choir ensemble. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
